{"cls":"level","html":"\n<div class=\"pagehead\" id=\"phT4\"><h1 class=\"pg-t\"><span class=\"pg-n\">5</span>Transformer block</h1><p class=\"pg-s\">Each Transformer block does two things.</p><details class=\"pg-more\"><summary aria-label=\"Expand notes for this stop\" title=\"Notes for this stop\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">ⓘ</span> Notes</summary><div class=\"ph-one\">Each Transformer block does two things: first words “look at” each other (attention), then each word “digests” on its own (FFN); residuals and normalization keep dozens of stacked layers trainable.</div><p class=\"ph-why\"><b>Why it’s designed this way: </b>Separating “exchanging information” from “processing individually” keeps the structure simple, endlessly stackable, and well suited to GPU parallelism.</p></details><div class=\"ph-top\"><span class=\"ph-lv\">Stop 5 of 11 </span><span>📍 App overview › Agent › LLM › Transformer block</span></div><div class=\"ph-map\" id=\"pmT4\"><span>On this page: </span><button class=\"\" data-sj=\"c_T4_0\" data-sp=\"T4\">Zooming into one T</button><button class=\"\" data-sj=\"c_T4_1\" data-sp=\"T4\">Each part in one s</button><button class=\"\" data-sj=\"c_T4_2\" data-sp=\"T4\">An analogy: a grou</button><button class=\"\" data-sj=\"c_T4_3\" data-sp=\"T4\">🧠 The logic under</button><button class=\"l3\" data-sj=\"labBlock\" data-sp=\"T4\">🧪 Build your own </button></div><div class=\"zoomnote\" id=\"znT4\" style=\"display:none\"></div></div><div class=\"m-stage\"><div class=\"m-dg main\"><div class=\"m-vbar\"><span class=\"m-vh\">👆 Tap a box for details<br>🤏 Pinch or double-tap</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"vz\" data-vz=\"out\" aria-label=\"Zoom out\">−</button><span class=\"vp\" aria-live=\"polite\">100%</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"vz\" data-vz=\"in\" aria-label=\"Zoom in\">＋</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"vz\" data-vz=\"reset\" aria-label=\"Reset\" disabled=\"\">⟲</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"vz\" data-vz=\"full\" aria-label=\"View full screen\">⛶</button></div><div class=\"diagram m-vw\"><svg id=\"svgL2\" viewBox=\"0 0 380 570\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" data-m=\"1\"><defs><marker id=\"ah2\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#94a3b8\"></path></marker><marker id=\"ar2\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#d97706\"></path></marker></defs><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"150\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\">⬇ One vector per word (from the previous layer)</text><g class=\"comp cat-attn\" data-id=\"attn\" data-train=\"yes\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Attention\"><rect class=\"main\" x=\"40\" y=\"50\" width=\"220\" height=\"80\" rx=\"12\"></rect><text class=\"t\" x=\"150\" y=\"79\">Attention</text><text class=\"s\" x=\"150\" y=\"99\">Words exchange information</text><text class=\"s\" x=\"150\" y=\"116\">(a meeting)</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"zm-h\">🔍</text><g class=\"badge b-train\"><rect x=\"100\" y=\"39\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f97316\"></rect><text x=\"150\" y=\"53\">🔥 Updated in training</text></g><g class=\"badge b-use\"><rect x=\"116\" y=\"39\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#0ea5e9\"></rect><text x=\"150\" y=\"53\">🔒 Read-only</text></g></g><g class=\"comp cat-norm\" data-id=\"addnorm\" data-train=\"part\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Residual + norm\"><rect class=\"main\" x=\"40\" y=\"170\" width=\"220\" height=\"70\" rx=\"12\"></rect><text class=\"t\" x=\"150\" y=\"202.5\">Residual + norm</text><text class=\"s\" x=\"150\" y=\"222.5\">Keep the draft + adjust the scale</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"zm-h\">🔍</text><g class=\"badge b-train\"><rect x=\"100\" y=\"159\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f97316\"></rect><text x=\"150\" y=\"173\">🔥 Few params updated</text></g><g class=\"badge b-use\"><rect x=\"116\" y=\"159\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#0ea5e9\"></rect><text x=\"150\" y=\"173\">🔒 Read-only</text></g></g><g class=\"comp cat-ffn\" data-id=\"ffn\" data-train=\"yes\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Feed-forward network\"><rect class=\"main\" x=\"40\" y=\"280\" width=\"220\" height=\"80\" rx=\"12\"></rect><text class=\"t\" x=\"150\" y=\"317.5\">Feed-forward network</text><text class=\"s\" x=\"150\" y=\"337.5\">Each word digests and draws on knowledge</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"352\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"zm-h\">🔍</text><g class=\"badge b-train\"><rect x=\"100\" y=\"269\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f97316\"></rect><text x=\"150\" y=\"283\">🔥 Updated in training</text></g><g class=\"badge b-use\"><rect x=\"116\" y=\"269\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#0ea5e9\"></rect><text x=\"150\" y=\"283\">🔒 Read-only</text></g></g><g><g class=\"comp cat-norm\" data-id=\"addnorm\" data-train=\"part\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Residual + norm\"><rect class=\"main\" x=\"40\" y=\"400\" width=\"220\" height=\"70\" rx=\"12\"></rect><text class=\"t\" x=\"150\" y=\"432.5\">Residual + norm</text><text class=\"s\" x=\"150\" y=\"452.5\">Keep the draft + adjust the scale</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"416\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"zm-h\">🔍</text><g class=\"badge b-train\"><rect x=\"100\" y=\"389\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f97316\"></rect><text x=\"150\" y=\"403\">🔥 Few params updated</text></g><g class=\"badge b-use\"><rect x=\"116\" y=\"389\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#0ea5e9\"></rect><text x=\"150\" y=\"403\">🔒 Read-only</text></g></g></g><path class=\"arrow \" d=\"M150 32 V39\" marker-end=\"url(#ah2)\"></path><path class=\"arrow \" d=\"M150 130 V157\" marker-end=\"url(#ah2)\"></path><path class=\"arrow \" d=\"M150 240 V267\" marker-end=\"url(#ah2)\"></path><path class=\"arrow \" d=\"M150 360 V387\" marker-end=\"url(#ah2)\"></path><path class=\"arrow \" d=\"M150 470 V506\" marker-end=\"url(#ah2)\"></path><path class=\"arrow res\" d=\"M150 40 H284 V205 H262\" marker-end=\"url(#ar2)\"></path><path class=\"arrow res\" d=\"M150 258 H284 V435 H262\" marker-end=\"url(#ar2)\"></path><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"292\" y=\"92\" fill=\"#b45309\">Residual: input</text><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"292\" y=\"110\" fill=\"#b45309\">skips attention</text><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"292\" y=\"128\" fill=\"#b45309\">directly</text><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"292\" y=\"312\" fill=\"#b45309\">Residual: input</text><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"292\" y=\"330\" fill=\"#b45309\">skips the FFN</text><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"292\" y=\"348\" fill=\"#b45309\">directly</text><path d=\"M34 50 H26 V470 H34\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"2\"></path><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"14\" y=\"260\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#0f766e\" font-weight=\"700\" transform=\"rotate(-90 14 260)\">× N layers (often dozens)</text><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"190\" y=\"530\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\">⬇ On to the next layer; the last layer’s output</text><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"190\" y=\"550\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\">goes to the “output scoring layer”</text></svg></div></div><details class=\"m-leg\"><summary>🎨 Legend: what the colours and dashed lines mean</summary><div class=\"legend\" id=\"legend2\"><span><i style=\"--c:var(--attn);--f:var(--attn-f)\"></i>Attention</span><span><i style=\"--c:var(--ffn);--f:var(--ffn-f)\"></i>Feed-forward network</span><span><i style=\"--c:var(--norm);--f:var(--norm-f)\"></i>Residual/norm</span><span><i class=\"dash\"></i>Dashed box = fixed computation/result, no learnable numbers</span></div></details></div><section class=\"card cc-closed\" id=\"trainPanel\" data-cc=\"1\">\n<h3 data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"🔁 (Training mode) How training works: loss → backpropagation → update parameters\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"cc-h\" aria-expanded=\"false\">🔁 (Training mode) How training works: loss → backpropagation → update parameters</button></h3><div class=\"cc-body\">\n<p class=\"lead\" data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"Training means drilling the model on huge amounts of text with “guess the next word” exercises: after each guess the answer is checked, the more wrong it was the bigger the penalty (the loss), and then every parameter is nudged a tiny bit in the direction that lowers the penalty. Repeat billions to trillions of times.\">Training means drilling the model on huge amounts of text with “guess the next word” exercises: after each guess the answer is checked, the more wrong it was the bigger the penalty (the loss), and then every parameter is nudged a tiny bit in the direction that lowers the penalty. Repeat billions to trillions of times.</p>\n<div class=\"m-dg\"><div class=\"m-vbar\"><span class=\"m-vh\">👆 Tap a box for details<br>🤏 Pinch or double-tap</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"vz\" data-vz=\"out\" aria-label=\"Zoom out\">−</button><span class=\"vp\" aria-live=\"polite\">100%</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"vz\" data-vz=\"in\" aria-label=\"Zoom in\">＋</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"vz\" data-vz=\"reset\" aria-label=\"Reset\" disabled=\"\">⟲</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"vz\" data-vz=\"full\" aria-label=\"View full screen\">⛶</button></div><div class=\"diagram m-vw\"><svg id=\"trainSvg\" viewBox=\"0 0 380 370\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" data-m=\"1\"><defs><marker id=\"aht\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#94a3b8\"></path></marker><marker id=\"art\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#d97706\"></path></marker></defs><g class=\"tnode\" id=\"tn0\"><rect x=\"22\" y=\"14\" width=\"160\" height=\"92\" rx=\"14\"></rect><text class=\"t\" x=\"102\" y=\"46\">① Forward pass</text><text class=\"s\" x=\"102\" y=\"70\">Model guesses next-word probabilities</text></g><g class=\"tnode\" id=\"tn1\"><rect x=\"204\" y=\"14\" width=\"160\" height=\"92\" rx=\"14\"></rect><text class=\"t\" x=\"284\" y=\"46\">② Check the answer</text><text class=\"s\" x=\"284\" y=\"70\">The correct next word is “good”</text></g><g class=\"tnode\" id=\"tn2\"><rect x=\"204\" y=\"142\" width=\"160\" height=\"92\" rx=\"14\"></rect><text class=\"t\" x=\"284\" y=\"174\">③ Compute the loss</text><text class=\"s\" x=\"284\" y=\"198\">loss = −log(p“good”)</text></g><g class=\"tnode\" id=\"tn3\"><rect x=\"204\" y=\"270\" width=\"160\" height=\"92\" rx=\"14\"></rect><text class=\"t\" x=\"284\" y=\"302\">④ Backpropagation</text><text class=\"s\" x=\"284\" y=\"326\">Works back through every parameter:</text><text class=\"s\" x=\"284\" y=\"344\">which way to adjust it</text></g><g class=\"tnode\" id=\"tn4\"><rect x=\"22\" y=\"270\" width=\"160\" height=\"92\" rx=\"14\"></rect><text class=\"t\" x=\"102\" y=\"302\">⑤ Update parameters</text><text class=\"s\" x=\"102\" y=\"326\">Every number in every table</text><text class=\"s\" x=\"102\" y=\"344\">moves one small step</text></g><path class=\"arrow flow\" d=\"M184 60 H202\" marker-end=\"url(#aht)\" style=\"stroke:#94a3b8\"></path><path class=\"arrow flow\" d=\"M284 106 V140\" marker-end=\"url(#aht)\" style=\"stroke:#94a3b8\"></path><path class=\"arrow flow\" d=\"M284 234 V268\" marker-end=\"url(#aht)\" style=\"stroke:#ea580c\"></path><path class=\"arrow flow\" d=\"M204 316 H184\" marker-end=\"url(#aht)\" style=\"stroke:#94a3b8\"></path><path class=\"arrow flow\" d=\"M44 270 V108\" marker-end=\"url(#aht)\" style=\"stroke:#f97316\"></path><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"56\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"12.5\" fill=\"#c2410c\">Next question,</text><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"56\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"12.5\" fill=\"#c2410c\">repeat billions of times 🔁</text></svg></div></div>\n<div class=\"two\">\n<div>\n<div class=\"row\"><button class=\"btn orange\" id=\"trainStep\" data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"Train one step ▶\">Train one step ▶</button><button class=\"btn ib\" id=\"trainReset\" data-l10n=\"\" data-i18n=\"reset\" data-ic=\"1\" aria-label=\"Reset\" title=\"Reset\">⟲</button><span class=\"tag demo\" data-l10n=\"\" data-i18n=\"sample_data\">Sample data</span></div>\n<p class=\"hint\" style=\"margin:6px 0 0\" data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"Exercise: “Today the weather is really ___”; the correct answer in the source text is &lt;b&gt;“good”&lt;/b&gt;.\">Exercise: “Today the weather is really ___”; the correct answer in the source text is <b>“good”</b>.</p>\n<div class=\"bars\" id=\"trainBars\"><div class=\"bar hit\"><span class=\"w\">good</span><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:14.0%\"></div></div><span class=\"p\">14%</span></div><div class=\"bar\"><span class=\"w\">bad</span><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:28.3%\"></div></div><span class=\"p\">28%</span></div><div class=\"bar\"><span class=\"w\">cold</span><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:23.2%\"></div></div><span class=\"p\">23%</span></div><div class=\"bar\"><span class=\"w\">hot</span><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:19.0%\"></div></div><span class=\"p\">19%</span></div><div class=\"bar\"><span class=\"w\">great</span><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:15.5%\"></div></div><span class=\"p\">16%</span></div></div>\n</div>\n<div>\n<div id=\"trainInfo\" class=\"formula\">Step <b>0</b>　Probability of the correct word “good”: <b>14%</b><br>Loss = −log(0.140) = <b style=\"color:#ea580c\">1.963</b><br><span class=\"hint\">At first the parameters are random, so the model is basically guessing, and even leans towards “bad”.</span></div>\n<svg id=\"lossChart\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 110\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:420px;background:#fff7ed;border-radius:10px\"><text x=\"8\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#9a3412\">Loss</text><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"95\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"95\" stroke=\"#fdba74\"></line><polyline points=\"20.0,16.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ea580c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"></polyline><circle cx=\"20.0\" cy=\"16.5\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#ea580c\"></circle><text x=\"290\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#9a3412\">Training steps →</text></svg>\n<p class=\"hint\" style=\"margin:4px 0 0\" data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"Loss = −log(probability of the correct word): giving the right answer 70% means a loss of about 0.36; giving it only 10% means about 2.3.\">Loss = −log(probability of the correct word): giving the right answer 70% means a loss of about 0.36; giving it only 10% means about 2.3.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"hint\" style=\"margin:10px 0 4px\" data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"Tap the cards below to see why the three training essentials are designed this way and why they work:\">Tap the cards below to see why the three training essentials are designed this way and why they work:</p>\n<div class=\"grid\" id=\"trainMinis\"><div class=\"mini\" data-id=\"data\" data-train=\"no\" style=\"--c:var(--io)\"><b>Massive data + next-word guessing</b><p>The training exercises: cut a passage from text and guess the word that follows.</p></div><div class=\"mini\" data-id=\"loss\" data-train=\"no\" style=\"--c:var(--out)\"><b>Loss (cross-entropy)</b><p>A single number: how badly this question was guessed.</p></div><div class=\"mini\" data-id=\"backprop\" data-train=\"no\" style=\"--c:var(--blk)\"><b>Backpropagation + gradient descent</b><p>Works out which way each parameter should move, then takes a small step.</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"note\" data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"Note: real training adjusts &lt;b&gt;all parameters&lt;/b&gt; (thousands up to hundreds of billions of numbers in all kinds of tables); the scores only change as a result. To keep it intuitive, this demo pushes the scores directly. Also, during training &lt;b&gt;every position in a sentence guesses its own next word at the same time&lt;/b&gt; (a “mask” stops it from peeking at the answer), so one sentence is many exercises at once.\">Note: real training adjusts <b>all parameters</b> (thousands up to hundreds of billions of numbers in all kinds of tables); the scores only change as a result. To keep it intuitive, this demo pushes the scores directly. Also, during training <b>every position in a sentence guesses its own next word at the same time</b> (a “mask” stops it from peeking at the answer), so one sentence is many exercises at once.</div>\n</div></section>\n<div class=\"subnav\"><span data-l10n=\"\" data-i18n=\"inside_the_transformer_block\">Inside the Transformer block:</span><button data-go=\"T4\" data-l10n=\"\" data-i18n=\"block_overview\" class=\"active\">Block overview</button><button data-go=\"T4a\" data-l10n=\"\" data-i18n=\"inside_attention\">Inside attention</button><button data-go=\"T4b\" data-l10n=\"\" data-i18n=\"feed_forward_and_output\">Feed-forward and output</button></div>\n<div class=\"card has-meta\" id=\"c_T4_0\" data-z=\"1\" data-zl=\"② Diagram\" data-nh=\"1\" data-cc=\"1\">\n<div class=\"cc-meta\"><span class=\"zl z2\">② Diagram</span></div><h2 data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"Zooming into one Transformer block\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"cc-h\" aria-expanded=\"true\">Zooming into one Transformer block</button></h2><div class=\"cc-body\">\n<p class=\"lead\" data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"The middle of an LLM is many “blocks” with exactly the same structure stacked on top of each other (real models often have dozens of layers). Each block has only two main steps: &lt;b&gt;attention&lt;/b&gt; (words talk to each other) and the &lt;b&gt;feed-forward network&lt;/b&gt; (each word digests on its own), and each step is followed by &lt;b&gt;residual + normalization&lt;/b&gt;.\" data-bz=\"1\">The middle of an LLM is many “blocks” with exactly the same structure stacked on top of each other (real models often have dozens of layers). Each block has only two main steps: <b>attention</b> (words talk to each other) and the <b>feed-forward network</b> (each word digests on its own), and each step is followed by <b>residual + normalization</b>.</p>\n\n\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"card has-meta cc-closed\" id=\"c_T4_1\" data-z=\"2\" data-zl=\"③ Details · why\" data-nh=\"1\" data-cc=\"1\">\n<div class=\"cc-meta\"><span class=\"zl zm\">③ Details · why</span></div><h3 data-l10n=\"\" data-i18n=\"each_part_in_one\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"cc-h\" aria-expanded=\"false\">Each part in one sentence</button></h3><div class=\"cc-body\">\n<div class=\"grid\" id=\"l2cards\"><div class=\"mini\" data-id=\"attn\" data-train=\"yes\" style=\"--c:var(--attn)\"><span class=\"hb b-train\">🔥 Updated in training</span><span class=\"hb b-use\">🔒 Read-only</span><b>Attention</b><p data-bz=\"1\">Words “take a look” at each other and exchange information.</p></div><div class=\"mini\" data-id=\"addnorm\" data-train=\"part\" style=\"--c:var(--norm)\"><span class=\"hb b-train\">🔥 Updated in training</span><span class=\"hb b-use\">🔒 Read-only</span><b>Residual + norm</b><p data-bz=\"1\">Residual: keep the draft and just add notes; normalization: bring the numbers back to a common scale</p></div><div class=\"mini\" data-id=\"ffn\" data-train=\"yes\" style=\"--c:var(--ffn)\"><span class=\"hb b-train\">🔥 Updated in training</span><span class=\"hb b-use\">🔒 Read-only</span><b>Feed-forward network</b><p data-bz=\"1\">Each word “digests and thinks” on its own, drawing on learned knowledge.</p></div><div class=\"mini\" data-id=\"blocks\" data-train=\"yes\" style=\"--c:var(--blk)\"><span class=\"hb b-train\">🔥 Updated in training</span><span class=\"hb b-use\">🔒 Read-only</span><b>N Transformer blocks</b><p data-bz=\"1\">This whole set is stacked many layers deep, each layer with its own tables</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"note\" data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"Did you know: the original 2017 paper did “compute first, then residual + normalization”; many models now “normalize first, then attention/feed-forward, then add the residual” (called Pre-Norm), which trains more stably. Same parts, slightly different order.\">Did you know: the original 2017 paper did “compute first, then residual + normalization”; many models now “normalize first, then attention/feed-forward, then add the residual” (called Pre-Norm), which trains more stably. Same parts, slightly different order.</div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"card has-meta cc-closed\" id=\"c_T4_2\" data-z=\"2\" data-zl=\"③ Details · why\" data-nh=\"1\" data-cc=\"1\">\n<div class=\"cc-meta\"><span class=\"zl zm\">③ Details · why</span></div><h3 data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"An analogy: a group of people reading a sentence together\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"cc-h\" aria-expanded=\"false\">An analogy: a group of people reading a sentence together</button></h3><div class=\"cc-body\">\n<div class=\"bz bzp\" style=\"margin:0\" data-bz=\"1\"><ul class=\"pts\"><li>Think of each word as a person.</li><li><b>Attention</b> = a short meeting where everyone listens to what the relevant people before them are saying</li><li>the <b>feed-forward network</b> = after the meeting everyone goes back to their desk and thinks it over with their own “knowledge base”</li><li>the <b>residual</b> = ideas are written as notes in the margin of the draft, which is always kept</li><li><b>normalization</b> = after each round the volume is set to the same level so nobody keeps getting louder.</li><li>Repeat “meeting + digesting” dozens of times and everyone understands the whole sentence more and more deeply.</li></ul></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"card has-meta cc-closed\" id=\"c_T4_3\" data-z=\"2\" data-zl=\"③ Details · why\" data-nh=\"1\" data-cc=\"1\">\n<div class=\"cc-meta\"><span class=\"zl zm\">③ Details · why</span></div><h3 data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"🧠 The logic underneath: why each step in the block is designed this way and why it works\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"cc-h\" aria-expanded=\"false\">🧠 The logic underneath: why each step in the block is designed this way and why it works</button></h3><div class=\"cc-body\">\n<div class=\"whylist\" data-ids=\"attn,ffn,residual,norm,blocks\"><details class=\"whyitem\" style=\"--c:var(--attn)\" open=\"\" data-dd=\"1\"><summary>Attention<span>Words “take a look” at each other and exchange information.</span></summary><div class=\"wi-act\"><button class=\"dd-c pri\" data-open=\"attn\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</i><span>Open the full card</span></button></div><div class=\"whyrow\"><div class=\"why\"><h4>🧠 Why it’s designed this way (the logic underneath)</h4><p data-bz=\"1\">A word’s meaning often depends on other words (is “Apple” the fruit or the phone?), and the related words may be far apart. Attention lets each word directly “look up” the whole preceding text and take information according to relevance — however far away, in a single step.</p></div><div class=\"eff\"><h4>✅ Why this works</h4><p data-bz=\"1\">All positions can be computed at the same time (unlike old recurrent networks that queue up one word at a time), which suits GPU parallelism perfectly, so large models can be trained on huge amounts of data; long-range relations are also less likely to get “lost”.</p></div></div><p class=\"lim\" data-bz=\"1\">⚠️ Limits / notes: The computation grows with the square of sentence length, so long texts are expensive; and “high attention weight = the model really relies on it to decide” doesn’t always hold.</p></details><details class=\"whyitem\" style=\"--c:var(--ffn)\" data-dd=\"1\"><summary>Feed-forward network<span>Each word “digests and thinks” on its own, drawing on learned knowledge.</span></summary><div class=\"wi-act\"><button class=\"dd-c pri\" data-open=\"ffn\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</i><span>Open the full card</span></button></div><div class=\"whyrow\"><div class=\"why\"><h4>🧠 Why it’s designed this way (the logic underneath)</h4><p data-bz=\"1\">Attention is essentially “mixing everyone’s value cards in proportion” (for the content it’s a weighted average, basically linear), so it can only move and mix information. A part with a non-linear switch is needed to process the information into new features and express complex rules like “if … then …”; without non-linearity, stacking any number of layers equals just one layer.</p></div><div class=\"eff\"><h4>✅ Why this works</h4><p data-bz=\"1\">Expanding and then compressing amounts to a very large “lookup + processing” unit: after expansion, thousands of detectors each recognize one pattern, and when one lights up it writes the matching information into the result. Many parameters, large capacity — it can remember a great many regularities.</p></div></div><p class=\"lim\" data-bz=\"1\">⚠️ Limits / notes: “Factual knowledge lives mainly in the feed-forward network” is an empirical observation from research (e.g. editing certain feed-forward parameters can change a fact the model remembers), not a rigorous proof; how knowledge is actually stored is still being researched.</p></details><details class=\"whyitem\" style=\"--c:var(--norm)\" data-dd=\"1\"><summary>Residual connection<span>Adds the step’s result to the original vector instead of replacing it.</span></summary><div class=\"wi-act\"><button class=\"dd-c pri\" data-open=\"residual\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</i><span>Open the full card</span></button></div><div class=\"whyrow\"><div class=\"why\"><h4>🧠 Why it’s designed this way (the logic underneath)</h4><p data-bz=\"1\">In a very deep network, the training signal from the last layer back to the first passes through dozens of multiplications and can easily shrink away (vanishing gradients) or get distorted; and if every layer rewrote the whole vector, the original information would easily be lost.</p></div><div class=\"eff\"><h4>✅ Why this works</h4><p data-bz=\"1\">Each layer only adds a small correction to the original vector, which leaves an “express lane”: gradients flow back to earlier layers almost unchanged and information isn’t lost. If a layer isn’t useful for now, it can just learn to “add 0” without breaking anything.</p></div></div><p class=\"lim\" data-bz=\"1\">⚠️ Limits / notes: This is a plain-language description of common practice; actual implementations vary by system.</p></details><details class=\"whyitem\" style=\"--c:var(--norm)\" data-dd=\"1\"><summary>Normalization<span>Brings a list of numbers to a common scale.</span></summary><div class=\"wi-act\"><button class=\"dd-c pri\" data-open=\"norm\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</i><span>Open the full card</span></button></div><div class=\"whyrow\"><div class=\"why\"><h4>🧠 Why it’s designed this way (the logic underneath)</h4><p data-bz=\"1\">As numbers are multiplied and added layer after layer they easily grow or shrink, making later computations (like softmax) extreme and sending the training signal out of control too.</p></div><div class=\"eff\"><h4>✅ Why this works</h4><p data-bz=\"1\">Pulling the values back into a common range each time keeps the scale of every layer’s input stable, so a larger learning rate can speed up training without making it collapse.</p></div></div><p class=\"lim\" data-bz=\"1\">⚠️ Limits / notes: There are several competing explanations of why normalization works so well, not yet fully settled; its benefits are mainly verified by experiment.</p></details><details class=\"whyitem\" style=\"--c:var(--blk)\" data-dd=\"1\"><summary>N Transformer blocks<span>Processes each word’s vector over and over so it “understands the context” better and better.</span></summary><div class=\"wi-act\"><button class=\"dd-c pri\" data-open=\"blocks\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</i><span>Open the full card</span></button></div><div class=\"whyrow\"><div class=\"why\"><h4>🧠 Why it’s designed this way (the logic underneath)</h4><p data-bz=\"1\">One round of “discuss + digest” only grasps shallow relations; stacking many layers lets later layers keep combining on top of earlier results, from words and phrases all the way to the meaning of the whole sentence. Every layer has the same structure, which simplifies design and allows large-scale parallelism on GPUs.</p></div><div class=\"eff\"><h4>✅ Why this works</h4><p data-bz=\"1\">With residuals and normalization standing guard, dozens of layers still train stably; empirically, more layers and parameters and more data mean better guesses (the so-called “scaling laws”).</p></div></div><p class=\"lim\" data-bz=\"1\">⚠️ Limits / notes: “Shallow layers handle grammar, deep layers handle meaning” is a common observation, not a strict division of labour; deeper isn’t always better — it also depends on the amount of data and training.</p></details></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"lab-divider\" data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"&lt;span&gt;🧪 Hands-on lab: Transformer block&lt;/span&gt;\" data-z=\"3\"><span>🧪 Hands-on lab: Transformer block</span></div>\n<div class=\"card lab has-meta\" id=\"labBlock\" data-z=\"3\" data-zl=\"🧪 Lab\" data-nh=\"1\">\n<div class=\"cc-meta\"><span class=\"zl z3\">🧪 Lab</span><span class=\"tag demo tag-s\" title=\"Simplified simulation: a random 16-dimensional mini network, not a real model\">Simplified simulation</span></div><h3 data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"🧪 Build your own Transformer block: toggle residual / normalization / feed-forward and stack many layers &lt;span class=&quot;tag demo&quot;&gt;Simplified simulation: a random 16-dimensional mini network, not a real model&lt;/span&gt;\">🧪 Build your own Transformer block: toggle residual / normalization / feed-forward and stack many layers</h3><p class=\"tag-note\" data-bz=\"1\">ⓘ Simplified simulation: a random 16-dimensional mini network, not a real model</p>\n<si-x data-si-tag=\"p\" class=\"lab-why bz\" data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"&lt;b&gt;Why it’s built this way: &lt;/b&gt;Blocks are stacked dozens deep. Every layer multiplies the numbers, and after many layers they either “blow up” (explode) or “shrink away” (vanish), so the early layers can’t learn. The residual provides a straight-through path and normalization pulls the scale back — they aren’t there to make it “smarter” but to make a deep stack “still trainable”.\" data-bz=\"1\"><ul class=\"pts\"><li><b>Why it’s built this way: </b>Blocks are stacked dozens deep.</li><li>Every layer multiplies the numbers, and after many layers they either “blow up” (explode) or “shrink away” (vanish), so the early layers can’t learn.</li><li>The residual provides a straight-through path and normalization pulls the scale back — they aren’t there to make it “smarter” but to make a deep stack “still trainable”.</li></ul></si-x>\n<div class=\"blk-sch\" id=\"bkSch\"></div>\n<div class=\"ctrls\">\n<label data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"&lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; id=&quot;bkRes&quot; checked&gt; ➕ Residual\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"bkRes\" checked=\"\"> ➕ Residual</label>\n<label data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"&lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; id=&quot;bkNorm&quot; checked&gt; 📏 Normalization\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"bkNorm\" checked=\"\"> 📏 Normalization</label>\n<label data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"&lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; id=&quot;bkAttn&quot; checked&gt; 👀 Attention (a random mixing table stands in here)\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"bkAttn\" checked=\"\"> 👀 Attention (a random mixing table stands in here)</label>\n<label data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"&lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; id=&quot;bkFfn&quot; checked&gt; 🧠 Feed-forward network\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"bkFfn\" checked=\"\"> 🧠 Feed-forward network</label>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ctrls\">\n<label data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"Layers &lt;input type=&quot;range&quot; id=&quot;bkL&quot; min=&quot;1&quot; max=&quot;64&quot; value=&quot;32&quot;&gt;&lt;b id=&quot;bkLV&quot;&gt;32&lt;/b&gt;\">Layers <input type=\"range\" id=\"bkL\" min=\"1\" max=\"64\" value=\"32\"><b id=\"bkLV\">32</b></label>\n<label data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"Init scale &lt;input type=&quot;range&quot; id=&quot;bkS&quot; min=&quot;0.5&quot; max=&quot;2&quot; step=&quot;0.05&quot; value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b id=&quot;bkSV&quot;&gt;1.00&lt;/b&gt;\">Init scale <input type=\"range\" id=\"bkS\" min=\"0.5\" max=\"2\" step=\"0.05\" value=\"1\"><b id=\"bkSV\">1.00</b></label>\n<button class=\"btn\" id=\"bkPlay\" data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"▶ Stack layer by layer\">▶ Stack layer by layer</button><button class=\"btn\" id=\"bkSeed\" data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"New random numbers\">New random numbers</button>\n</div>\n<canvas id=\"bkChart\" class=\"chart\" height=\"230\"></canvas>\n<div class=\"formula\" id=\"bkInfo\"></div>\n<div class=\"lab-obs bz\" data-l10n=\"\" data-en=\"&lt;b&gt;👀 Try this: &lt;/b&gt;① All on: signals and gradients stay fairly steady. ② Turn off normalization: with the residual the numbers accumulate layer by layer and keep growing. ③ Turn off the residual but keep normalization: the forward pass is flattened, but gradients flowing back shrink or grow layer by layer. ④ Turn both off and set the init scale to 0.7 or 1.4: things vanish or explode quickly. ⑤ Turn off the feed-forward network: the signal looks normal, but the block loses its “digesting” step and can learn far less (the curves here can’t show that).\" data-bz=\"1\"><div class=\"bz-h\"><b>👀 Try this: </b></div><ul class=\"pts\"><li>① All on: signals and gradients stay fairly steady.</li><li>② Turn off normalization: with the residual the numbers accumulate layer by layer and keep growing.</li><li>③ Turn off the residual but keep normalization: the forward pass is flattened, but gradients flowing back shrink or grow layer by layer.</li><li>④ Turn both off and set the init scale to 0.7 or 1.4: things vanish or explode quickly.</li><li>⑤ Turn off the feed-forward network: the signal looks normal, but the block loses its “digesting” step and can learn far less (the curves here can’t show that).</li></ul></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card quiz has-meta\" id=\"quizT4\" data-sec=\"T4\" data-z=\"3\" data-zl=\"❓ Quiz\" data-nh=\"1\"></div>\n<!--m2h--><nav class=\"m-hand\" aria-label=\"Where next\"><p class=\"mh-t\">🧭 Where next</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"mh-b dn\" data-go=\"T4a\"><span class=\"mh-k\">⬇ Go deeper</span><b>Attention</b><span class=\"mh-r\">Step one in the block: attention</span></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"mh-b dn\" data-go=\"T4b\"><span class=\"mh-k\">⬇ Go deeper</span><b>FFN &amp; output</b><span class=\"mh-r\">Step two: feed-forward and output</span></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"mh-b up\" data-go=\"T3\"><span class=\"mh-k\">⬆ One level up</span><b>LLM</b><span class=\"mh-r\">Where the block sits in the LLM pipeline</span></button><p class=\"mh-c\"><span>🧪 Labs on this page:</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"mh-x\" data-sj=\"labBlock\" data-sp=\"T4\">Build your own Trans</button></p><p class=\"mh-c\"><span>Concepts used here, explained elsewhere:</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"mh-x\" data-open=\"embed\">Embedding table</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"mh-x\" data-open=\"kVec\">Vectors &amp; dot product</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"mh-x\" data-open=\"kSoft\">Softmax</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"mh-x\" data-open=\"kProb\">Distributions &amp; expectation</button></p></nav><!--/m2h-->\n<div class=\"ph-nav m-pn\" data-sec=\"T4\"><div class=\"pn-row\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"pn-b\" data-go=\"N\" aria-label=\"Previous stop: Neural Network Basics\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M15 5l-7 7 7 7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"></path></svg></button><div class=\"pn-dots\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"dt  v\" data-go=\"T1\" aria-label=\"Word  1 : App overview\"><i></i></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"dt  v sub\" data-go=\"T2\" aria-label=\"Word  2 : Agent\"><i></i></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"dt  v sub\" data-go=\"T3\" aria-label=\"Word  3 : LLM\"><i></i></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"dt  v sub\" data-go=\"N\" aria-label=\"Word  4 : Neural Network Basics\"><i></i></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"dt on v\" data-go=\"T4\" aria-label=\"Word  5 : Transformer block (current)\"><i></i></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"dt  sub\" data-go=\"T4a\" aria-label=\"Word  6 : Attention\"><i></i></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"dt \" data-go=\"T4b\" aria-label=\"Word  7 : FFN &amp; output\"><i></i></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"dt \" data-go=\"T5\" aria-label=\"Word  8 : MoE &amp; efficiency\"><i></i></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"dt \" data-go=\"T6\" aria-label=\"Word  9 : Multimodal\"><i></i></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"dt \" data-go=\"T7\" aria-label=\"Word  10 : Training &amp; RL\"><i></i></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"dt \" data-go=\"T8\" aria-label=\"Word  11 : Reference &amp; map\"><i></i></button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"pn-b pri\" data-go=\"T4a\" aria-label=\"Next stop: Attention\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M9 5l7 7-7 7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"></path></svg></button></div><p class=\"pn-cap\">5 / 11 · Next stop: <button type=\"button\" class=\"pn-l\" data-go=\"T4a\">Attention ›</button></p></div>"}
